# SGC203 event-ignored — `[Shop]` sends `<A>` then `<C>` (async `~>`). Per-sender
# FIFO lands `<A>` first, taking `{M}` to `X`, where `<C>` has no transition.
# The run judges `<C>` against that heading state; the check must not replay the
# in-flight `<A>` a second time (it would step X -<A>-> Z -<C>-> W, no drop).
# The static half still guesses an order from the two emits (info, as in
# trace-205-fifo).
# expect: error:14:SGC203
# expect: info:14:SGC205
#!spec
(User) -> [Shop] : go()
[Shop] ~> <A>
[Shop] ~> <C>
state {M} {
  + -<A>-> X
  X -<A>-> Z
  Z -<C>-> W
}
